TYPE=string
GROUP=statute
DOC=WHICH STATUTES GET FULL TEXT AT SUMMON. render_memories renders these in complete
DEFAULT<<'SPIRA_CONF_DEFAULT_EOF'
    # WHICH STATUTES GET FULL TEXT AT SUMMON. render_memories renders these in complete
    # paragraph form; everything else is rendered as a slug-only index line. Seeded from
    # citation frequency in commits and bead text (measured 2026-09-11): those cited most
    # often are the ones a violation costs most to miss. Being wrongly in core costs ~88
    # words; being wrongly out costs an untraced violation. The default is generous.
    # CSV of slug names, without the leading path — e.g. "law-foo,law-bar".
    # THREE SLUGS DROPPED (sp-crr3n), never shipped in spira/statutes/: this default is what
    # ops, groomer, maechen, batcher and spike (no FAYTH_STATUTE_CORE of their own) fall back
    # to, and a fresh install died pre-session on these ("core statute(s) declared but not
    # found", acceptance phase B). law-fence-loops-on-shared-hardware names this operator's
    # own gt dashboard and pokedumpster by name; law-gate-earns-its-place and
    # law-arm-before-you-retire name Ryan in their own scars — all inventory, not mechanism
    # (law-harness-ships-mechanism-not-inventory).
    : "${SPIRA_STATUTE_CORE:=law-absence-needs-a-positive-control,law-alerts-must-be-actionable,law-prefer-the-real-dependency,law-gates-run-in-a-clean-environment,law-closed-is-not-landed,law-a-regression-test-must-be-seen-to-fail,law-guard-binds-the-caller,law-verify-nothing-was-dropped,law-hand-land-the-unblocker,law-no-close-reason-admits-unfinished}"
SPIRA_CONF_DEFAULT_EOF
